        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0451" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/512.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Memorandum; in reply to the first of those of November
                    25.]</p>
                <p>The Department of State is in receipt of the memorandum of his excellency the
                    Mexican ambassador in which he advises [etc.].</p>
                <p>This memorandum has been communicated to the Department of Justice for such
                    action as it may deem appropriate.</p>
                <p>The department in this connection desires to invite the attention of his
                    excellency the Mexican ambassador to the closing portion of its memorandum of
                    this date regarding the proper procedure in case the Mexican Government is in
                    possession of evidence showing that the neutrality laws of the United States
                    have been violated.</p>


                <xi:include href="d482-a1.xml" xpointer="d482-a1"/>
